ipedia.org%3ATime+ball" class="Z3988" about="#mwt84" id="mwAro"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-25" id="cite_note-25" data-mw-footnote-number="25"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwArs"><a href="#cite_ref-25" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwArw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAr0">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-25" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt88" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwAr4" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite news ","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"https://www.newspapers.com/article/newsday-titanic-memorial-in-new-york-cit/137185187/"},"title":{"wt":"1913: Titanic Memorial Lighthouse Commemorates Victims of Ocean Tragedy"},"newspaper":{"wt":"[[Newsday]]"},"date":{"wt":"24 August 2005"},"accessdate":{"wt":"21 December 2023"},"via":{"wt":"[[Newspapers.com]]"},"quote":{"wt":"From 1913 until 1967 a black &apos;time ball&apos; at the top activated by a telegraphic signal from the National Observatory in Washington DC dropped at noon every day signaling the time to ships in the harbor."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt88" id="mwAr8"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.newspapers.com/article/newsday-titanic-memorial-in-new-york-cit/137185187/" class="external text" id="mwAsA">"1913: Titanic Memorial Lighthouse Commemorates Victims of Ocean Tragedy"</a>. <i id="mwAsE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newsday" title="Newsday" id="mwAsI">Newsday</a></i>. 24 August 2005<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwAsM">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwAsQ">21 December</span> 2023</span> <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAsU">–</span> via <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newspapers.com" title="Newspapers.com" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAsY">Newspapers.com</a>. <q id="mwAsc">From 1913 until 1967 a black 'time ball' at the top activated by a telegraphic signal from the National Observatory in Washington DC dropped at noon every day signaling the time to ships in the harbor.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Newsday&amp;rft.atitle=1913%3A+Titanic+Memorial+Lighthouse+Commemorates+Victims+of+Ocean+Tragedy&amp;rft.date=2005-08-24&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.newspapers.com%2Farticle%2Fnewsday-titanic-memorial-in-new-york-cit%2F137185187%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATime+ball" class="Z3988" about="#mwt88" id="mwAsg"></span></span></li>
